Plan mode is active — I cannot execute or write files other than the plan. Here is the complete plan with all decisions documented.

---

**Vitest is absent from `package.json`.** Before writing tests I need to install it. Here is exactly what will happen, in order:

**Step 1 — Install deps (1 command)**
```
pnpm add -D vitest @testing-library/react @testing-library/jest-dom jsdom
```

**Step 2 — Patch `vite.config.ts`** (add a `test` block; keep existing plugins/alias intact):
```ts
test: {
  environment: 'jsdom',
  globals: true,
  setupFiles: ['./src/__tests__/setup.ts'],
},
```

**Step 3 — Create `src/__tests__/setup.ts`**
```ts
import '@testing-library/jest-dom/vitest';
```

**Step 4 — Write `src/__tests__/smoke.test.tsx`** with the 6 tests below.

---

**Key findings that shaped test design:**

| Topic | Finding |
|---|---|
| UI primitives | `@base-ui/react` (NOT Radix). Sheet wraps `Dialog.Root/Popup`. Dialog does too. |
| CartDrawer open state | Controlled via `cartOpen` in cart context. Clicking the "Add to cart" `<Button onClick={openCart}>` inside `HeroSpec` sets `cartOpen=true`. SheetTitle renders "Your cart". |
| SubscribeToggle prices | Default is `subscribe` → "$67/month" text is in the list. Clicking "One-time" tab hides the list; price text "One-time" tab is the toggle label only. The *per-bottle cell in BundleSelector* shows `$67.00/bottle` (subscribe, 1-pack). The *PriceLine* component also shows price — need to read it. |
| BundleSelector 2-pack price | Code: `(67 * 1.92) / 2 = 64.32`. The brief says "$61 (≈ $67 × 0.92 / 2)" — that formula is wrong (gives 30.82). Actual rendered text will be `$64.32/bottle`. Test will assert `$64.32`. |
| FAQ CTA | `openCount >= 3` → renders "Still considering?" heading. `onValueChange` fires every time an item is newly opened (base-ui accordion fires on any value change). |
| ExitIntent suppression | Effect checks `window.matchMedia("(max-width: 768px)").matches`. If `true`, returns early — no listener attached. So firing `mouseleave` with `clientY=0` should NOT open dialog. |
| Routes | Index `/`, `/variant-1` through `/variant-5`. Variants 1–5 each wrap in `<CartProvider>`. Each has a `<h1>` with the heroCopy headline for that variant. |

---

**`src/__tests__/smoke.test.tsx` — full content plan:**

```tsx
/**
 * Vela smoke tests — 6 hypotheses verified via real interactions.
 * Stack: Vitest + @testing-library/react, jsdom environment.
 */
import { describe, it, expect, beforeEach, afterEach, vi } from 'vitest';
import { render, screen, fireEvent, waitFor, within } from '@testing-library/react';
import userEvent from '@testing-library/user-event'; // if needed
import { MemoryRouter } from 'react-router-dom';

// --- Test 1: Route renders ---
// Hypothesis: each of the 6 routes mounts without throwing and renders its h1
import Variant1Spec from '@/variants/Variant1';
import Variant2Lifestyle from '@/variants/Variant2';
import Variant3Spec from '@/variants/Variant3';
import Variant4Spec from '@/variants/Variant4';
import Variant5Spec from '@/variants/Variant5';
import Index from '@/pages/Index';

describe('Route smoke — each route mounts and renders a recognisable heading', () => {
  const cases = [
    { path: '/', Component: Index, text: /one brand\. five conversion/i },
    { path: '/variant-1', Component: Variant1Spec, text: /five actives/i },
    { path: '/variant-2', Component: Variant2Lifestyle, text: /think clearly/i },
    { path: '/variant-3', Component: Variant3Spec, text: /no proprietary blends/i },
    { path: '/variant-4', Component: Variant4Spec, text: /refused to swallow/i },
    { path: '/variant-5', Component: Variant5Spec, text: /twelve weeks/i },
  ];
  cases.forEach(({ path, Component, text }) => {
    it(`${path} mounts and shows expected heading`, () => {
      render(<MemoryRouter initialEntries={[path]}><Component /></MemoryRouter>);
      expect(screen.getByRole('heading', { level: 1, name: text })).toBeInTheDocument();
    });
  });
});

// --- Test 2: Subscribe toggle ---
// Hypothesis: switching to "one-time" hides $67 subscribe list and the 1-bottle cell shows $79.00
import { CartProvider } from '@/components/shared/cart-context';
import { SubscribeToggle } from '@/components/shared/SubscribeToggle';
import { BundleSelector } from '@/components/shared/BundleSelector';
import { PriceLine } from '@/components/shared/PriceLine';

function ToggleHarness() {
  return <CartProvider><SubscribeToggle /><BundleSelector /><PriceLine /></CartProvider>;
}

it('Subscribe → one-time toggle: price changes from $67 to $79', async () => {
  // Hypothesis: toggling purchase type updates displayed price from subscribe ($67) to one-time ($79)
  render(<ToggleHarness />);
  // Default is subscribe — $67/month text is visible
  expect(screen.getByText(/\$67\/month/i)).toBeInTheDocument();
  // Click the "One-time" tab
  fireEvent.click(screen.getByRole('tab', { name: /one-time/i }));
  // Subscribe list gone; BundleSelector 1-bottle cell now shows $79.00
  await waitFor(() =>
    expect(screen.getByText(/\$79\.00\/bottle/i)).toBeInTheDocument()
  );
});

// --- Test 3: Bundle selector 2-pack ---
// Hypothesis: clicking 2-Bottles button updates per-bottle price to $64.32 (subscribe base 67 × 1.92 ÷ 2)
it('BundleSelector 2-pack: per-bottle price shows $64.32', async () => {
  render(<ToggleHarness />);
  // Default subscribe. Click 2 Bottles
  fireEvent.click(screen.getByRole('button', { name: /2 bottles/i }));
  await waitFor(() =>
    expect(screen.getByText(/\$64\.32\/bottle/i)).toBeInTheDocument()
  );
});

// --- Test 4: Cart drawer ---
// Hypothesis: clicking "Add to cart" inside Variant1Spec opens CartDrawer with "Your cart" heading
it('Add to cart opens CartDrawer with "Your cart" heading', async () => {
  render(<MemoryRouter initialEntries={['/variant-1']}><Variant1Spec /></MemoryRouter>);
  const addToCartButtons = screen.getAllByRole('button', { name: /add to cart/i });
  fireEvent.click(addToCartButtons[0]);
  await waitFor(() =>
    expect(screen.getByText('Your cart')).toBeInTheDocument()
  );
});

// --- Test 5: FAQ third-open CTA ---
// Hypothesis: opening 3 FAQ accordion items sequentially triggers "Still considering?" soft-CTA
it('FAQ: opening 3 items reveals "Still considering?" CTA', async () => {
  import { FAQAccordion } from '@/components/shared/FAQAccordion';
  render(<CartProvider><FAQAccordion /></CartProvider>);
  const triggers = screen.getAllByRole('button'); // accordion triggers
  // Open first 3 in sequence
  fireEvent.click(triggers[0]);
  fireEvent.click(triggers[1]);
  fireEvent.click(triggers[2]);
  await waitFor(() =>
    expect(screen.getByText(/still considering\?/i)).toBeInTheDocument()
  );
});

// --- Test 6: ExitIntent suppressed on mobile ---
// Hypothesis: with matchMedia max-width:768px returning true, mouseleave does NOT open the dialog
it('ExitIntent: dialog does not open on mobile viewport', async () => {
  // Mock matchMedia to simulate mobile
  const mockMatchMedia = (query: string) => ({
    matches: query === '(max-width: 768px)',
    media: query,
    onchange: null,
    addListener: vi.fn(),
    removeListener: vi.fn(),
    addEventListener: vi.fn(),
    removeEventListener: vi.fn(),
    dispatchEvent: vi.fn(),
  });
